Z||000000||SeanyD||06-25-2000||03:12 PM||||I have an 85 2.8 and an 84 2.5 ..both need work before they see the road again...but the 84 has much more potential. so what could fit from the 85??  could I take the whole rear end of the 85 along with the computer and instuments and stuff them in the 84?? and would the driver side rear wheel bearing be the same on both cars??||||reg||5
Z||000001||batboy||06-25-2000||10:36 PM||||Most stuff should be the same. The wheel bearings are the same. I think the deck lid and louvers are different and the engine wiring harness is different too. At least I think the bulkhead is mounted differently. I'd build the 85 V6, it'll be worth more.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||06-26-2000||11:57 AM||||Unless, of course, the '84 is an Indy in which case that's the one to rebuild.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Gold-86SE||06-26-2000||12:04 PM||||<BR>In your opinion what makes the 84 have more potential than the 85?<P>Options? Like, pl, pm, pw, cruise, etc.<P>Overall condition of the car?  Like, good body, good paint, etc.<P>If you are looking for economy instead of performance the 2.5 is good, if you want performance then you are better off working on the 2.8.<P>Also consider this, if there are things on the 84 that you like, you can almost with certainty carry them over to the 85.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||06-26-2000||07:27 PM||||Maybe it's just me, but there's just enough little things that make the 84 an oddball. A similarly equipped 85 in similar overall condition, but with a V6, will always be worth more than a plain ol' 84. Now all the 84 lovers will throw rocks at me.||||reg||1
Z||000005||SeanyD||06-26-2000||10:28 PM||||the 84 has it's sstrong point's like the bodys in better condition, the sunroof, power windows and all that...but the 4 is really gutless....hence the want to put a 6 in it....but I've figured why not restore both now...sell em...and try to pick up this very nice 86 not far from here!||||reg||1
